1
00:00:12,125 --> 00:00:14,125
When did I fall asleep?

2
00:00:14,166 --> 00:00:17,125
The pact shouldn't have expired yet.

3
00:00:22,083 --> 00:00:23,125
Sir Piggymaru?

4
00:00:23,125 --> 00:00:25,000
What's the matter?

5
00:00:26,166 --> 00:00:28,166
What's up, Piggymaru?

6
00:00:28,208 --> 00:00:31,000
Oh, did I wake you?

7
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,041
Nah, don't worry about it.

8
00:00:36,166 --> 00:00:39,083
The resident of this room might be out.

9
00:00:40,125 --> 00:00:42,000
Did you hear that just now?

10
00:00:42,041 --> 00:00:43,000
Yes.

11
00:00:44,083 --> 00:00:45,208
- Get back!
- Right!

12
00:00:54,125 --> 00:00:56,041
A skeleton king!

13
00:00:56,125 --> 00:00:57,166
This thing?

14
00:00:58,083 --> 00:01:00,208
It's leagues above the other monsters here.

15
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,041
Sir Hati!

16
00:01:02,041 --> 00:01:03,125
We should be able to slay it

17
00:01:03,166 --> 00:01:06,166
if we shatter that silver part below its chin!

18
00:01:06,166 --> 00:01:08,000
That's its weak spot, huh?

19
00:01:08,041 --> 00:01:11,166
This monster is too much
for your average soldier to handle.

20
00:01:11,166 --> 00:01:14,125
It's so strong that even the Saber Tigers

21
00:01:14,166 --> 00:01:16,166
might just barely be able to take it.

22
00:01:19,166 --> 00:01:23,083
Looks like it considers Mist
the real threat here.

23
00:01:24,125 --> 00:01:26,083
Now, how shall we attack?

24
00:01:26,166 --> 00:01:29,125
Sir Hati, I have a request.

25
00:01:29,125 --> 00:01:32,000
I'm about to use a certain power

26
00:01:32,041 --> 00:01:36,041
to improve my base physical abilities
and create unique armaments.

27
00:01:36,083 --> 00:01:39,125
I'd like to keep this power
a secret as long as I can,

28
00:01:39,166 --> 00:01:44,041
so could you please keep what
you're about to witness between us?

29
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:46,208
Yeah, this thing's definitely strong.

30
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,041
Also, my apologies in advance.

31
00:01:49,083 --> 00:01:52,000
Should this monster exceed my expectations,

32
00:01:52,041 --> 00:01:54,125
I might not be able to protect you.

33
00:01:54,125 --> 00:01:57,041
So if it comes down to it, please run—

34
00:01:57,041 --> 00:01:58,041
Paralyze!

35
00:02:02,125 --> 00:02:05,125
Rather, it's only strong compared
to the rest of these ruins.

36
00:02:05,166 --> 00:02:06,125
Poison!

37
00:03:49,166 --> 00:03:53,041
THE CHAIN KNOWN AS TRUST

38
00:03:53,041 --> 00:03:55,166
Good. Looks like this was the right thing.

39
00:03:55,208 --> 00:04:00,166
You mean that skeleton king was the monster
you were searching for, Sir Hati?

40
00:04:00,208 --> 00:04:01,166
Yeah.

41
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:05,166
Once we return to the surface,

42
00:04:05,166 --> 00:04:07,208
I'll answer any questions I can.

43
00:04:08,208 --> 00:04:10,125
Did my face give me away?

44
00:04:12,208 --> 00:04:14,041
What's up, Piggymaru?

45
00:04:16,041 --> 00:04:17,208
There's something over there?

46
00:04:31,166 --> 00:04:32,166
What's this?

47
00:04:36,041 --> 00:04:38,125
Some kind of magic cloth or something?

48
00:04:39,166 --> 00:04:40,166
An egg?

49
00:04:41,125 --> 00:04:42,208
What is it, Piggymaru?

50
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:44,125
You're interested in the egg?

51
00:04:45,125 --> 00:04:47,000
You want to take it home with us?

52
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:49,000
All right.

53
00:04:49,041 --> 00:04:51,125
If that's what you want,
I'll see what I can do.

54
00:04:52,125 --> 00:04:55,000
Well, shall we head back to the surface now?

55
00:04:56,041 --> 00:04:58,041
It's skeleton knights!

56
00:04:58,166 --> 00:04:59,125
Run!

57
00:05:05,041 --> 00:05:07,000
This isn't happening! It can't be!

58
00:05:07,041 --> 00:05:09,000
- I lost my hand!
- Sakura-san, hang in there!

59
00:05:09,083 --> 00:05:12,083
Th-The goddess might heal it for you!

60
00:05:15,083 --> 00:05:16,208
Can I do it with this weapon?

61
00:05:16,208 --> 00:05:18,125
No, I must!

62
00:05:18,166 --> 00:05:22,000
- I have to buy time for
everyone to escape and—
- Hands off, Ayaka!

63
00:05:22,125 --> 00:05:24,000
Bullet!

64
00:05:24,083 --> 00:05:26,041
RED FIST SHOT
BULLET

65
00:05:28,166 --> 00:05:30,000
Draconic Buster!

66
00:05:30,041 --> 00:05:31,208
GOLDEN DRAGON BLAST
DRACONIC BUSTER

67
00:05:38,041 --> 00:05:41,166
There's no denying they're strong foes.

68
00:05:41,166 --> 00:05:45,041
However, I was simply stronger.

69
00:05:45,208 --> 00:05:48,125
With that, I've reached level 24.

70
00:05:52,125 --> 00:05:55,166
I-Is this the Dragon Eye Chalice?!

71
00:05:55,166 --> 00:05:57,208
Is it actually the real thing?!

72
00:06:02,041 --> 00:06:06,166
At any rate, this concludes
my business in the Mils Ruins.

73
00:06:06,166 --> 00:06:08,000
Sir Hati!

74
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:11,125
I was watching from afar,

75
00:06:11,125 --> 00:06:13,041
but that was quite a commotion.

76
00:06:14,083 --> 00:06:18,166
There's going to be a reception tomorrow
where I receive my reward.

77
00:06:18,208 --> 00:06:20,125
I'll find an inn for another night.

78
00:06:20,125 --> 00:06:23,208
Then I assume you're free
until the reception tomorrow?

79
00:06:23,208 --> 00:06:24,166
Yes.

80
00:06:24,208 --> 00:06:27,000
If possible, I'd like to speak to you alone.

81
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:29,000
Would either of our rooms work for you?

82
00:06:29,125 --> 00:06:30,208
I don't mind that.

83
00:06:31,166 --> 00:06:34,000
Then how about mine at eight o'clock?

84
00:06:34,208 --> 00:06:37,041
You make decisions swiftly, don't you?

85
00:06:37,041 --> 00:06:38,166
I'll be there.

86
00:06:40,041 --> 00:06:44,041
Once again, thank you very much
for the Dragon Eye Chalice.

87
00:06:44,166 --> 00:06:47,083
Nothing you need to thank me for.

88
00:06:56,125 --> 00:06:59,125
So we have a monster enhancement
solution now, do we?

89
00:06:59,208 --> 00:07:02,041
We'll be using this on you later.

90
00:07:03,125 --> 00:07:05,166
Sir Hati, it's me, Mist.

91
00:07:06,166 --> 00:07:09,000
She's here right at the agreed time.

92
00:07:10,083 --> 00:07:13,166
You want to employ me as your bodyguard?

93
00:07:13,208 --> 00:07:17,000
Yeah, I thought you might be
interested in earning a bit more.

94
00:07:17,041 --> 00:07:19,083
Though maybe you're set on travel funds now

95
00:07:19,125 --> 00:07:22,083
with the reward for the Dragon Eye Chalice.

96
00:07:22,083 --> 00:07:25,208
Indirectly reminding her about that...

97
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:27,208
Even I feel like this is playing dirty.

98
00:07:30,125 --> 00:07:32,125
You've probably guessed as much,

99
00:07:32,125 --> 00:07:35,041
but my goal is finding the Witch of Taboos.

100
00:07:35,125 --> 00:07:38,125
My destination is the Land
of Golden-Eyed Monsters.

101
00:07:38,125 --> 00:07:40,125
The Land of Golden-Eyed Monsters...

102
00:07:40,166 --> 00:07:43,125
I'm expecting plenty
of swarming monster attacks.

103
00:07:43,166 --> 00:07:47,041
I'd feel better having a skilled
swordsman watching my back,

104
00:07:48,041 --> 00:07:50,166
just like when we were
conquering the Mils Ruins.

105
00:07:50,208 --> 00:07:55,083
I've been considering hiring a warrior
all along to ensure my safety,

106
00:07:55,125 --> 00:07:57,083
and you're a perfect fit.

107
00:07:57,166 --> 00:08:00,208
I'm on a journey to the Duchy of Yonato.

108
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:03,041
If we head there via the
Land of Golden-Eyed Monsters,

109
00:08:03,083 --> 00:08:05,083
that'd be quite convenient for me.

110
00:08:05,208 --> 00:08:06,208
However...

111
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:08,208
I'm a little hesitant to agree,

112
00:08:08,208 --> 00:08:11,166
but I have to accept it's necessary
to meet her needs.

113
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:13,208
No reason to rush the decision.

114
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:16,208
It sounds like there are other routes
if you're headed to Yonato.

115
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:18,166
By the way, can I ask something, Seras?

116
00:08:18,208 --> 00:08:20,208
Yes. What is it?

117
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:21,208
Oh!

118
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:25,125
E-Er, Sir Hati, um, why did you just...

119
00:08:25,166 --> 00:08:28,125
Sorry for catching you off guard.

120
00:08:28,208 --> 00:08:30,125
So you knew?

121
00:08:30,166 --> 00:08:32,166
Remember falling asleep in the Mils Ruins?

122
00:08:32,166 --> 00:08:34,166
That was the work of my skill.

123
00:08:34,208 --> 00:08:36,166
It was, was it?

124
00:08:37,083 --> 00:08:41,083
You were hesitating earlier
about revealing yourself to me, weren't you?

125
00:08:41,208 --> 00:08:46,083
Traveling together while trying
to hide your identity would be an issue.

126
00:08:46,083 --> 00:08:48,125
Because you can't exactly sleep that way.

127
00:08:48,166 --> 00:08:49,125
Am I wrong?

128
00:08:49,125 --> 00:08:51,041
Y-You're not.

129
00:08:51,041 --> 00:08:53,166
I need your combat prowess.

130
00:08:53,208 --> 00:08:55,041
I've no intent to sell you out.

131
00:08:55,208 --> 00:08:59,041
I use the power of spirits
to conceal my identity.

132
00:08:59,125 --> 00:09:03,000
It requires that I offer up
my desire for sleep in exchange.

133
00:09:03,083 --> 00:09:06,000
Which is why you revert back
to normal when you sleep.

134
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:07,000
Yes.

135
00:09:07,125 --> 00:09:10,041
I was being chased by those Holy Watchers

136
00:09:10,041 --> 00:09:13,083
because they caught me unawares
and saw my true form.

137
00:09:13,125 --> 00:09:18,000
I have a lot more flexibility in my travels
with those four gone.

138
00:09:18,041 --> 00:09:20,208
I truly am grateful to you.

139
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:23,000
If you're dismissing your spell around me,

140
00:09:23,125 --> 00:09:26,083
I assume that means you trust me?

141
00:09:26,083 --> 00:09:28,208
Yes, I do, Sir Hati.

142
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:32,166
I believe you are a man worthy of trust.

143
00:09:32,208 --> 00:09:34,125
Trust, huh?

144
00:09:35,208 --> 00:09:37,125
- It's Touka.
- Huh?

145
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:40,083
My real name is Touka Mimori.

146
00:09:40,208 --> 00:09:43,083
Please don't share that with anyone else.

147
00:09:43,125 --> 00:09:47,000
In return, I won't reveal your name
to anyone without your consent either.

148
00:09:47,125 --> 00:09:51,083
This is another way to further
bind her to me using trust.

149
00:09:51,125 --> 00:09:54,000
Hati... No, Sir Tooka.

150
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:56,041
Let me introduce myself again.
I am Seras Ashrain.

151
00:09:56,083 --> 00:09:58,166
ELF, FORMER CAPTAIN OF NEAH'S KNIGHTS
- I will serve as your bodyguard

152
00:09:58,166 --> 00:10:01,000
and accompany you to the
Land of Golden-Eyed Monsters.

153
00:10:01,041 --> 00:10:03,000
Yeah, I'll be counting on you.

154
00:10:03,041 --> 00:10:04,000
Yes.

155
00:10:05,166 --> 00:10:07,041
Here's your payment.

156
00:10:12,041 --> 00:10:13,166
Terribly sorry.

157
00:10:14,083 --> 00:10:15,083
Everything all right?

158
00:10:15,166 --> 00:10:18,041
Um, I was just surprised...

159
00:10:18,083 --> 00:10:19,083
By what?

160
00:10:19,125 --> 00:10:23,125
Sir Tooka, I don't think this could be
anything other than a blue dragon gem.

161
00:10:24,041 --> 00:10:25,083
Blue dragon gem?

162
00:10:27,166 --> 00:10:29,208
Is it something valuable?

163
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:33,125
It's said that these gems are only rarely born

164
00:10:33,125 --> 00:10:36,125
within legendary blue-eyed dragons.

165
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:40,041
There's nary a one circulating
on the market right now.

166
00:10:40,083 --> 00:10:41,125
Its value...

167
00:10:41,208 --> 00:10:45,125
easily surpasses the reward
for the Dragon Eye Chalice.

168
00:10:45,208 --> 00:10:48,041
Then it should be satisfactory payment.

169
00:10:48,041 --> 00:10:50,000
You can't, Sir Tooka!

170
00:10:50,208 --> 00:10:54,000
You shouldn't give something
like this away so readily.

171
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:57,000
Too nice for her own good too, huh?

172
00:11:03,083 --> 00:11:05,125
I said it was yours.

173
00:11:05,125 --> 00:11:06,166
Toss it out if you want.

174
00:11:06,208 --> 00:11:09,041
Huh? Wait, but...

175
00:11:09,083 --> 00:11:12,000
It's sufficient payment
for guarding me, right?

176
00:11:12,041 --> 00:11:14,125
Th-That's true, but...

177
00:11:15,041 --> 00:11:16,083
Very well.

178
00:11:16,083 --> 00:11:19,083
For the time being, please call me
Hati in front of other people.

179
00:11:19,083 --> 00:11:21,083
I'll call you Mist when we're outside too.

180
00:11:21,083 --> 00:11:22,166
Understood.

181
00:11:22,208 --> 00:11:25,125
It might be a little late at this point...

182
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:29,041
But as you know, I'm on the run.

183
00:11:29,083 --> 00:11:33,041
There's a great deal about me
that I haven't told you yet.

184
00:11:33,125 --> 00:11:36,125
I'm not trying to dig into your past.

185
00:11:37,083 --> 00:11:41,166
As your employer, I just want you
to be in top form as my guard.

186
00:11:42,166 --> 00:11:45,041
I have no intention to pry past that.

187
00:11:45,208 --> 00:11:49,166
You're always considerate
in that fashion, Sir Tooka.

188
00:11:50,125 --> 00:11:52,041
Yeah, well, I'm a nice guy.

189
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:04,208
Perhaps I should have cleansed myself
before meeting with Sir Tooka earlier.

190
00:12:10,083 --> 00:12:12,041
Tooka Mimori...

191
00:12:13,041 --> 00:12:16,083
I'm not trying to dig into your past.

192
00:12:21,083 --> 00:12:22,125
I want to believe him,

193
00:12:22,125 --> 00:12:24,083
like I did the princess.

194
00:12:30,041 --> 00:12:31,125
Hey, check it out!

195
00:12:31,166 --> 00:12:34,208
Looks like some mercenary's
already won her over.

196
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:39,041
I heard she was spotted
leaving his room last night.

197
00:12:39,041 --> 00:12:40,125
Let them say what they will.

198
00:12:40,125 --> 00:12:44,041
- So she discovered a taste for men
alongside the Dragon Eye Chalice, eh?
- You're quite mature about that, Sir Hati.

199
00:12:44,041 --> 00:12:47,041
By the way, have you ever
heard of forbidden magic?

200
00:12:47,125 --> 00:12:49,041
Yes, I have.

201
00:12:49,041 --> 00:12:51,041
First unimportant discovery:

202
00:12:51,041 --> 00:12:55,000
Seras apparently has a tendency
to touch her chest while talking.

203
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:58,166
Said magic is forbidden according
to Goddess Vicius.

204
00:12:59,041 --> 00:13:03,125
It's generally understood
to be specific ancient spells.

205
00:13:03,208 --> 00:13:04,208
In other words,

206
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:08,000
these spells are now forbidden
because the goddess said so.

207
00:13:08,083 --> 00:13:12,083
Indeed, we can assume they are
forbidden by her decree.

208
00:13:12,125 --> 00:13:14,125
Magic the goddess outlawed...

209
00:13:14,166 --> 00:13:18,041
That's bound to mean it's
spells that are dangerous to her.

210
00:13:18,125 --> 00:13:22,083
My apologies. That's about all I know.

211
00:13:22,125 --> 00:13:24,041
No, that's plenty.

212
00:13:24,041 --> 00:13:25,041
Thank you.

213
00:13:25,041 --> 00:13:28,083
I-If I managed to be of help, I'm glad.

214
00:13:28,166 --> 00:13:31,166
Need you be so deferential
over a simple thanks?

215
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:37,041
I think it's the first time you've
given me a frank thank you.

216
00:13:37,041 --> 00:13:40,000
I was feeling a bit bashful.

217
00:13:42,041 --> 00:13:44,083
They said it would be a morning reception.

218
00:13:44,125 --> 00:13:47,083
I should be back by one
in the afternoon at the latest.

219
00:13:47,208 --> 00:13:50,041
Then I'll be outside the inn
a little after noon.

220
00:13:50,125 --> 00:13:51,125
Very well.

221
00:13:51,166 --> 00:13:53,208
I shall see you then, Sir Hati.

222
00:14:04,208 --> 00:14:08,000
All right, let's start the enhancement
experiment, Piggymaru.

223
00:14:21,166 --> 00:14:23,125
Thank you all for gathering here today!

224
00:14:23,208 --> 00:14:26,083
I have invited a mage specialized
in breaking illusions

225
00:14:26,083 --> 00:14:29,166
so that we can ensure the authenticity
of the Dragon Eye Chalice,

226
00:14:29,166 --> 00:14:32,208
recently recovered by Mist Balukas.

227
00:14:33,041 --> 00:14:35,041
Now, let's have a look!

228
00:14:52,041 --> 00:14:53,125
Seras...

229
00:14:58,125 --> 00:15:03,000
ALION CASTLE
- I heard you had a tough time when
the skeleton knights appeared.

230
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:05,208
Um, what about Sakura-san?

231
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:08,000
Yes, I'll take care of her.

232
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:10,041
I'll put her back together with Heal.

233
00:15:10,041 --> 00:15:12,166
I see. You have my thanks.

234
00:15:12,208 --> 00:15:15,083
I can't use it on just anyone, though.

235
00:15:15,125 --> 00:15:18,083
This is only because Miss Sakura is B-class.

236
00:15:19,083 --> 00:15:20,166
By the way, Miss Sogou,

237
00:15:20,208 --> 00:15:23,166
will you not be joining
Mister Kirihara's group?

238
00:15:30,083 --> 00:15:34,125
I can't imagine I'd get along very
well with Kirihara-kun as things stand.

239
00:15:34,125 --> 00:15:36,041
That's what I mean.

240
00:15:36,208 --> 00:15:42,083
I'm saying your selfishness is
disrupting the harmony of Class 2-C.

241
00:15:42,083 --> 00:15:44,125
At least from what I've seen.

242
00:15:44,166 --> 00:15:46,083
M-My selfishness?

243
00:15:46,125 --> 00:15:48,208
Oh, dearie me. Am I wrong?

244
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:51,208
Is there some rational explanation?
Are you okay?

245
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:54,083
I-It's not like that! I just...

246
00:15:54,125 --> 00:15:56,041
No, no, it's fine.

247
00:15:56,041 --> 00:16:00,166
This is all the result
of insufficient guidance.

248
00:16:01,041 --> 00:16:04,041
The blame is entirely on me.

249
00:16:04,166 --> 00:16:05,208
Miss Sogou?

250
00:16:06,125 --> 00:16:08,041
I'm sorry.

251
00:16:08,041 --> 00:16:09,166
Even if it is selfish,

252
00:16:09,208 --> 00:16:12,125
I can't team up with Kirihara-kun
as he is now.

253
00:16:12,208 --> 00:16:16,166
Even if that means turning your back
on a world seeking salvation?

254
00:16:17,083 --> 00:16:20,125
I'm fulfilling my duty as an
S-Class hero in my own way!

255
00:16:21,166 --> 00:16:22,208
Very well!

256
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:27,041
Then I'll entrust the students who couldn't
pass their trials to you, Miss Sogou.

257
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:30,000
If an S-Class like you trains them,

258
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:32,083
I'm sure they'll become
as strong as a hundred men.

259
00:16:32,125 --> 00:16:34,083
Hold on just a minute!

260
00:16:34,083 --> 00:16:39,208
We already settled this matter when
I agreed to fight in their stead, right?!

261
00:16:39,208 --> 00:16:43,125
To be honest, we received
a royal decree a few days ago

262
00:16:43,166 --> 00:16:47,041
calling for the disposal
of all heroes who can't fight.

263
00:16:47,083 --> 00:16:50,208
I'm sorry, but I'm powerless to change it.

264
00:16:51,041 --> 00:16:54,125
If I refuse, you'll get rid
of them, won't you?

265
00:16:54,125 --> 00:16:57,125
That's what I'll be forced to do. I'm sorry.

266
00:16:58,041 --> 00:16:59,208
I understand.

267
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:01,208
Excellent! Take good care of them.

268
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:04,083
I'll share the details with you later.

269
00:17:04,083 --> 00:17:05,125
Excuse me.

270
00:17:06,083 --> 00:17:09,041
Oh, and just in case...

271
00:17:09,166 --> 00:17:11,166
Know that if they become a hindrance,

272
00:17:11,208 --> 00:17:15,041
you may be forced to reckon
with a cruel reality.

273
00:17:15,083 --> 00:17:16,166
But I'm sure you'll be fine.

274
00:17:16,166 --> 00:17:19,083
Humans always grow stronger
when they face reality.

275
00:17:19,166 --> 00:17:22,000
I thank you for your concern.

276
00:17:32,166 --> 00:17:34,125
That damn bitch.

277
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:38,083
Either I misjudged her,

278
00:17:38,166 --> 00:17:41,125
or something has happened to Seras.

279
00:17:41,166 --> 00:17:43,083
What's your wager?

280
00:17:44,125 --> 00:17:48,125
If you think she ditched us
without a word, squeal twice.

281
00:17:48,125 --> 00:17:50,125
If you think otherwise, squeal once.

282
00:17:51,208 --> 00:17:55,208
Sounds like we're both leaning
toward a generous read this time.

283
00:17:55,208 --> 00:17:57,125
Not much of a bet that way.

284
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:01,041
Seras hardly has a motive to disappear on us.

285
00:18:01,041 --> 00:18:02,125
If she didn't want to go with us,

286
00:18:02,166 --> 00:18:05,125
she could've just turned down
the gig to start with.

287
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:07,125
- And if she meant to deceive us,
- Hey, did you hear?

288
00:18:07,125 --> 00:18:09,041
- she wasted way too much effort.
- The woman who found that Dragon Eye Chalice
was the fugitive Princess Knight!

289
00:18:09,083 --> 00:18:11,125
The woman who found that Dragon Eye Chalice
was the fugitive Princess Knight!

290
00:18:11,208 --> 00:18:13,083
Yeah, I heard.

291
00:18:13,083 --> 00:18:15,125
Apparently she fled into the Dark Forest.

292
00:18:15,125 --> 00:18:17,125
Let's go! It's paladin hunting time!

293
00:18:17,166 --> 00:18:18,166
I wouldn't do that!

294
00:18:18,166 --> 00:18:20,166
Huh? Why would you say that?

295
00:18:20,208 --> 00:18:23,083
You don't want to get involved.

296
00:18:31,125 --> 00:18:32,083
The—

297
00:18:32,125 --> 00:18:34,000
The Black Dragon Knights?!

298
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:41,041
THE DARK FOREST

299
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:45,083
The Black Dragon Knights!

300
00:18:51,083 --> 00:18:53,208
Willozega, Willozega!

301
00:18:55,166 --> 00:18:57,000
Silfigzea!

302
00:19:10,125 --> 00:19:14,083
Thanks to that illusion breaker,
my spirit of light is disoriented.

303
00:19:14,166 --> 00:19:16,166
I can't transform until it recovers.

304
00:19:16,208 --> 00:19:18,125
Just surrender and die,

305
00:19:18,125 --> 00:19:20,083
Seras Ashrain!

306
00:19:26,125 --> 00:19:29,041
If their average knight is this skilled,

307
00:19:29,041 --> 00:19:31,000
what are the troops above them like?

308
00:19:36,083 --> 00:19:37,125
No.

309
00:19:37,166 --> 00:19:39,000
The dragon behind me is a decoy!

310
00:19:39,041 --> 00:19:40,125
My real enemy...

311
00:19:40,166 --> 00:19:42,041
is in front of me!

312
00:19:42,125 --> 00:19:44,208
Well done seeing through that!

313
00:19:44,208 --> 00:19:46,083
My name is Gizun!

314
00:19:46,083 --> 00:19:50,166
I'm vice captain of the squad led
by Sir Orban of the Five Dragoons!

315
00:19:52,166 --> 00:19:55,125
You die here, Seras Ashrain!

316
00:19:55,125 --> 00:19:57,166
I can't use my Spirit Regalia right now.

317
00:19:57,166 --> 00:20:00,125
I'll have to manage with my available spirits.

318
00:20:03,083 --> 00:20:05,166
I thought they would try and take me captive.

319
00:20:05,208 --> 00:20:09,041
Has their stance finally
changed to eliminating me?

320
00:20:09,041 --> 00:20:10,166
If you want to know, fine.

321
00:20:10,166 --> 00:20:12,166
Shall I tell you before you die?

322
00:20:13,041 --> 00:20:17,000
Orban's squad is under secret orders.

323
00:20:18,125 --> 00:20:21,125
You may have features as enticing as honey

324
00:20:21,166 --> 00:20:24,208
and a body that stokes the instincts of men...

325
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:30,125
but even so, there are still people
in this world who'd see you dead!

326
00:20:31,125 --> 00:20:35,000
I knew it. I'll need my
Spirit Regalia for this foe.

327
00:20:38,083 --> 00:20:39,041
Oh no!

328
00:20:46,208 --> 00:20:49,041
If you're going to kill me,
then make it quick.

329
00:20:49,083 --> 00:20:52,041
We were told to kill you without
doing anything to you,

330
00:20:52,083 --> 00:20:54,125
but rejoice, Princess Knight of a lost nation.

331
00:20:54,125 --> 00:20:56,166
If you haven't known a man yet,

332
00:20:56,166 --> 00:21:00,125
then I'll show you what it means
to be with one before you die!

333
00:21:01,125 --> 00:21:04,000
If only I could use my Spirit Regalia!

334
00:21:04,125 --> 00:21:05,125
Paralyze.

335
00:21:06,125 --> 00:21:08,208
Now, time to have some f—

336
00:21:12,041 --> 00:21:13,041
Hey.

337
00:21:13,083 --> 00:21:16,000
It's long past the time we agreed to meet.

338
00:21:19,166 --> 00:21:20,166
Poison!

339
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:26,125
INFLICT POISON, POISON
LETHAL

340
00:21:26,166 --> 00:21:27,125
INFLICT POISON, POISON
NONETHAL

341
00:21:27,125 --> 00:21:28,166
Too—

342
00:21:29,125 --> 00:21:32,000
What are you doing here?

343
00:21:32,083 --> 00:21:34,208
I came looking for you, of course.

344
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:37,166
That's not what I'm asking about.

345
00:21:37,208 --> 00:21:38,166
Hold on.

346
00:21:39,083 --> 00:21:40,083
Sleep.

347
00:21:42,083 --> 00:21:46,166
We may have things to talk about that
we don't want anyone overhearing.

348
00:21:47,041 --> 00:21:49,125
I-I'm sorry I didn't consider that.

349
00:21:49,166 --> 00:21:52,166
However, if you remain with me, then...

350
00:21:52,166 --> 00:21:55,125
I'll be pursued by the
Black Dragon Knights too?

351
00:21:55,125 --> 00:21:57,041
Th-That's right!

352
00:21:57,083 --> 00:21:59,041
I'll return the payment you gave me.

353
00:21:59,083 --> 00:22:01,125
So let's nullify our bodyguard agreement.

354
00:22:01,166 --> 00:22:03,208
To be honest, it would be a pain.

355
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:08,041
I-Indeed. Staying with me
will only cause you trouble.

356
00:22:08,041 --> 00:22:10,000
That's not what I meant.

357
00:22:11,208 --> 00:22:14,000
U-Um, what is this?

358
00:22:14,125 --> 00:22:15,125
Open it and see.

359
00:22:17,125 --> 00:22:20,125
A-Are these all blue dragon gems?!

360
00:22:20,125 --> 00:22:21,125
Well, yeah.

361
00:22:21,166 --> 00:22:24,041
You really are...

362
00:22:24,041 --> 00:22:27,083
I meant it'd be a pain to find a better guard.

363
00:22:28,125 --> 00:22:29,166
Now, Seras...

364
00:22:30,083 --> 00:22:32,000
Take off your clothes.

365
00:22:34,166 --> 00:22:35,166
Huh?

366
00:24:10,166 --> 00:24:14,208
HUMANITY'S STRONGEST, CIVIT GARTLAND

